# Host-card: meta-repo path (`~/git` vs worktree)

This window is a **host-card** workspace. The meta-repo root in the workspace is the
folder named **`git`** (card worktree under
`~/.local/share/workvm/host-cards/<project>/<id>/worktree/git`), **not** the live
checkout at `~/git`.

## Always

- Create/update/delete versioned meta-repo files **only** under that workspace
  `git/` tree (`project.conf`, `workspace.code-workspace`, `*/prompts/`,
  `.cursor/rules`, `HISTORICO.md`, overlay, sandbox defs, layout rules, …).
- When a prompt or habit says `~/git/...`, **resolve** it to the same path under
  the open workspace `git/` folder (same idea as `host-card-e2e-path` for e2e).

## Never (unless the user asks explicitly)

- Do **not** edit bare `~/git/...` (or `/home/**/git/...` outside the card
  worktree) for meta-repo content — even if the path is writable and “is the
  live project”. That duplicates state, skips the card worktree, and often
  triggers “outside workspace” permission prompts.
- Do **not** “sync both” (`~/git` + worktree) on your own. One write target:
  the open workspace `git/` worktree.

## Exception

- Change files under bare `~/git` **only** when the user **explicitly** asks to
  edit `~/git` (or the live checkout) in that message.

## Still OK without that exception

- **Run** scripts/binaries from `~/git/bin/…` / `workvm-host-card` / compose that
  already expect `GIT_ROOT=~/git`.
- **Clone** product repos into `~/git/<project>/…` when `CLONE_REPOS` /
  `project-setup` say so (clones are gitignored runtime trees). The
  *definition* that lists those clones (`project.conf`, workspace) still lives
  in the card `git/` worktree.
